Except as provided herein the city clerk may not accept or process an alcoholic beverage license application for a location that is associated with a license that is suspended, revoked or expired pursuant to section 2.5-16 through 2.5-219. An alcoholic beverage license application for such location may be accepted and processed by the city clerk if the business at such location is sold pursuant to a bona fide sale at fair market value to a person or entity with no direct or indirect relationship to the holder, or equity owner of the holder if the holder is not an individual, of the suspended, revoked or expired alcoholic beverage license at that location. Conditions precedent to the acceptance and processing of a license at such location shall be the delivery of the following documents to the city clerk:
(1) Copy of the sales contract for the business.
(2) Sworn affidavit of seller, or all equity owners of seller if seller is not an individual, that the:
a. Sale price represents the fair market value of the business;
b. Affiant does not have and will not have an interest in business of the applicant buyer;
c. Affiant is not a relative of the buyer or any equity owner of buyer, if applicable; and
d. Affiant will receive no payment from the buyer other than as set forth in the sales contract.
(3) Sworn affidavit of buyer, or all equity owners of buyer if buyer is not an individual, that the:
a. Sale price represents the fair market value of the business;
b. Affiant has never had an interest in business of the seller;
c. Affiant is not a relative of the seller or any equity owner of seller, if applicable; and seller, and the equity owners of seller, if applicable, will receive no payment from the buyer other than as set forth in the sales contract.
(Ord. of 6-20-2022(1), § 2)

